Q: Regex to match and capture a word A: <blockquote>
<p>find and capture a word that contains the sequence &quot;fp&quot;, &quot;fd&quot;, &quot;sp&quot; or
&quot;sd&quot; in a sentence. However, the word may contain some non-word
characters like θ or ð.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You should match Unicode letters <code>\p{L}</code> instead of regular word characters <code>\w</code>:</p>
<p><a href="https://regex101.com/r/MdjQnf/2" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>\p{L}*[fs][pd]\p{L}*</code></a></p>
<p>Click on the pattern to try it online. I have simplified the pattern.</p>
<pre><code>use warnings;
use strict;

use utf8;
use open &quot;:std&quot;, &quot;:encoding(UTF-8)&quot;;

my @regex = qr/\p{L}*[fs][pd]\p{L}*/mp;
my @strs = 'fpgθ tig &lt;br/&gt;
tig gfpθ tig&lt;br/&gt;
tig gθfp&lt;br/&gt;
fptig gfpθ tig&lt;br/&gt;
sddgsdθ(θ@) tig gθfp&lt;br/&gt;';

for (@strs) 
{
    my @m = /@regex/gm;
    print &quot;@m&quot; if @m;   # No space allowed by the pattern
}
</code></pre>

Q: How to test if specific attribute exists in XML node? A: <pre><code>using System.Xml.Linq;

namespace XmlParsing
{
    internal class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            var xml = &quot;&quot;&quot;
                &lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;utf-8&quot;?&gt;
                &lt;root id=&quot;abc&quot;&gt;
                &lt;/root&gt;
                &quot;&quot;&quot;;

            var document = XDocument.Parse(xml);
            var root = document.Root;
            if (root == null) {
                Console.WriteLine(&quot;\&quot;root\&quot; element not found&quot;);
                return;
            }

            var idAttr = root.Attribute(&quot;id&quot;);
            if (idAttr == null) {
                Console.WriteLine(&quot;\&quot;id\&quot; attribute not found&quot;);
                return;
            }

            var idStr = idAttr.Value;
            if (!long.TryParse(idStr, out long idVal)) {
                Console.WriteLine(&quot;\&quot;id\&quot; attribute has no value&quot;);
                return;
            }

            Console.WriteLine($&quot;\&quot;id\&quot; attribute has value \&quot;{idVal}\&quot;&quot;);
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
